---
id: PY-003
type: rule
family: python-reliability
title: '# pylint: disable suppression'
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 3

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.py]
allowlist: ['**/test_*.py', '**/*_test.py', '**/tests/**', '**/conftest.py', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '#\s*pylint:\s*disable'

related: [PY-001, PY-002]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

This `# pylint: disable` turns the linter off with no inline justification of
why the warning is wrong here. Prefer fixing the flagged code; if the warning
is a genuine false positive, record why with a reason suppression:
`# @anvil-ignore PY-003 -- dynamic attr set by the ORM metaclass`.
